"""Summoner subclasses, last seven (Summoner 2024). Own wording."""
SUB = {
"Bond of the Aberrant Psion": {"spab": "CHA",
 "f": {
  "Psychic Spells": "At the Summoner levels in the table you always have these spells prepared. Level 3: Dissonant Whispers, Sleep. Level 5: Detect Thoughts, Suggestion. Level 7: Summon Aberration. Level 9: Hunger of Hadar, Sending. Level 13: Confusion. Level 17: Synaptic Static, Telekinesis.",
  "Psychic Eidolon": "Your Eidolon is an alien being whose look you describe. **Changes.** Its type is Aberration. Strength 8 (-1), Dexterity 14 (+2), Constitution 16 (+3), and its Intelligence equals its Charisma. It is proficient in Arcana and Insight and resists Psychic damage. **Psychic Attacks.** It gains Ranged Attacker for free, not counting against its Evolutions, and its Conjured Strike can deal Psychic damage. **Telepathic Link (cost 1 AP).** It extends your telepathic bond to another creature it can see within 30 feet of itself. You and the Eidolon can talk telepathically with that creature for 10 minutes, until it uses this action again, or until it ends the link with no action.",
  "Divination Expert": "Conjuration Expert also covers Divination spells. Wizard Divination spells are added to your Summoner spell list.",
  "Telekinetic Eidolon": "Your Eidolon gains the action Telekinetic Movement (cost 1+ AP). It moves a Medium or smaller creature within 30 feet up to 20 feet to an unoccupied space it can see. An unwilling creature makes a Constitution save against your spell save DC and resists the move on a success. Each AP spent beyond the first adds 10 feet. Uses equal your Charisma modifier (minimum 1). A Long Rest restores all.",
  "Mind Blast": "Your Eidolon gains the action Mind Blast (cost 2 AP). Each creature of its choice in a 30-foot Cone makes an Intelligence save against your spell save DC. On a failure a creature takes 3d6 plus your Summoner level Psychic damage, cannot take Reactions until the start of your next turn, and on its next turn must pick one of its action, Bonus Action, or movement and can do only that. On a success it takes half damage. After one use, it cannot be used again until a Short or Long Rest, unless you expend a level 3+ spell slot (no action) to restore it.",
  "Psychic Marker": "When a creature fails an Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma save against one of your spells or your Eidolon's abilities, you can place a psychic marker in its mind. It lasts 1d4 days. It ends early if you mark another creature or leave the target's plane. Remove Curse, Greater Restoration, or Wish also ends it. After you mark a creature, you cannot do so again until a Long Rest. While a creature is marked you gain these. **Mind Reading.** You can cast Detect Thoughts on it from any distance without sight of it, and it has Disadvantage on the save. **Precognition.** It has Disadvantage on attacks against you, and you have Advantage on saves against effects it creates. **Psychic Rend.** As a Magic action you destroy the marker. The target makes an Intelligence save or takes 8d10 Psychic damage and is Stunned until the end of your next turn. On a success it takes half damage only."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Telekinetic Eidolon", "n": "Telekinetic Movement", "lvl": 6, "max": "mod:CHA", "reset": "long", "tag": "1+ AP"},
        {"feature": "Mind Blast", "lvl": 10, "max": 1, "reset": "short", "tag": "2 AP"},
        {"feature": "Psychic Marker", "lvl": 14, "max": 1, "reset": "long", "tag": "Mark"}],
 "acts": {"Psychic Marker": "action"},
 "fx": [[3, "Psychic Eidolon", {"notes": [["Note", "Eidolon resists Psychic damage and gains Ranged Attacker for free"]]}]]},

"Bond of the Living Armament": {"spab": "CHA",
 "f": {
  "Armament Spells": "At the Summoner levels in the table you always have these spells prepared. Level 3: Magic Missile, Shield. Level 5: Cloud of Daggers, Magic Weapon. Level 7: Summon Construct. Level 9: Elemental Weapon, Conjure Barrage. Level 13: Death Ward. Level 17: Animate Objects, Steel Wind Strike.",
  "Armament Eidolon": "In a 1-hour ritual, which you can do during a Short or Long Rest, you bind your Eidolon to one Simple or Martial melee weapon and one suit of armor. Whenever you manifest it afterward, it appears as that armor wielding that weapon, and the gear vanishes with it when it dissipates. **Changes.** Strength 16 (+3), Dexterity 13 (+1), Constitution 14 (+2). It is Immune to Poison damage and the Poisoned condition. Its AC is as if it wore the armor, unless already higher. Its Conjured Strike uses the weapon, including the weapon's damage die, damage type, and properties, magical or not. If the weapon or armor is magical, the Eidolon gains what a wearer would, and must attune if required. **Equip/Unequip (cost 1 AP).** The Eidolon equips itself onto your body while within 5 feet of you. Then you gain all its Speed. It moves with you and can act normally, but cannot use Conjured Strike unless you have hands free to wield its weapon. Any attack that would target you targets it instead. For other effects, the creator picks you or the Eidolon. When you make a D20 Test, you can use either its bonus or yours. **Evolution interactions.** Ranged Attacker lets you bind a ranged weapon instead, and Conjured Strike becomes a ranged attack at the weapon's normal range with no ammunition needed. Strike Mastery adds the bound weapon's mastery property to the choices.",
  "Encase": "Your Eidolon gains the action Encase (cost 2 AP). One creature within 5 feet of its size or smaller makes a Strength save against your spell save DC. On a failure the Eidolon equips itself onto the target for 1 minute, filling its space. The target is Restrained, its AC becomes the Eidolon's AC, it moves with the Eidolon, and whenever the Eidolon takes damage, the damage is halved and the rest hits the target. The target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success. The Eidolon can also unequip as a Bonus Action at no AP cost. When it ends, the Eidolon appears within 5 feet of the target. After a success it cannot use this again until a Short or Long Rest, unless you expend a level 2+ spell slot (no action) to restore it.",
  "Enhanced Protection": "**Flying Equip.** The Eidolon can use Equip/Unequip and Encase from up to 30 feet away, and when it unequips from a creature it appears within 30 feet of that creature without provoking Opportunity Attacks. **Quick Equip.** It can use Equip as a Reaction when you are targeted by an attack.",
  "Autopilot": "You can no longer sacrifice your action to give your Eidolon AP. Instead it gains 2 AP at the start of each of its turns, even if you are Incapacitated. You also always have Contingency prepared and can cast it with your Conjuration Expert slots."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Encase", "lvl": 6, "max": 1, "reset": "short", "tag": "2 AP"}],
 "acts": {"Encase": "other"}},

"Bond of the Mirror Mage": {"spab": "CHA",
 "f": {
  "Mirror Spells": "At the Summoner levels in the table you always have these spells prepared. Level 3: Disguise Self, Silent Image. Level 5: Mirror Image, Misty Step. Level 9: Counterspell, Major Image. Level 13: Dimension Door, Phantasmal Killer. Level 17: Circle of Power, Wall of Force.",
  "Mirror Eidolon": "Your Eidolon is a slightly translucent living illusion that copies you. **Changes.** Its type matches yours. Its Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution equal yours. It gains your skill proficiencies, Species traits, and Feats. Any of those with limited uses share their uses with you. **Illusory Defense (Reaction).** Trigger: it is targeted by an attack, or you are targeted by an attack while within 5 feet of it. Response: the attack has Disadvantage.",
  "Illusion Expert": "Conjuration Expert also covers Illusion spells. Wizard Illusion spells are added to your Summoner spell list.",
  "Reflected Positioning": "Your Eidolon gains Tethered Space for free, not counting against its Evolutions. It can use Swap Places as a Bonus Action.",
  "Focal Point": "When you cast a spell on a creature standing at the midpoint of the line between you and your Eidolon, you can apply one effect. Uses equal your Charisma modifier (minimum 1). A Long Rest restores all. **Save Penalty.** The target subtracts a d6 from its saves against the spell this turn. **Attack Bonus.** You add a d6 to your attack rolls with the spell against the target this turn. **Extra Damage.** The first time the target takes damage from the spell this turn, add your Summoner level to the damage.",
  "Magical Reflection": "When you or your Eidolon succeed on a save against a spell or magical effect, or are missed by an attack from one, you can use your Reaction to reflect it onto a different creature you can see within 30 feet of you or the Eidolon, whoever was targeted. After a success you cannot use this again until a Short or Long Rest. **Saving throw.** The new target must succeed on the same kind of save against your spell save DC or be affected. If the effect needs Concentration, you must concentrate. **Attack roll.** Make a ranged spell attack against the new target. On a hit it is affected by the attack that missed."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Focal Point", "lvl": 10, "max": "mod:CHA", "reset": "long", "tag": "Spell rider"},
        {"feature": "Magical Reflection", "lvl": 14, "max": 1, "reset": "short", "tag": "Reaction"}],
 "acts": {"Magical Reflection": "reaction"}},

"Bond of the Monster Shaper": {"spab": "CHA",
 "f": {
  "Monstrous Spells": "At the Summoner levels in the table you always have these spells prepared. Level 3: Expeditious Retreat, Jump. Level 5: Alter Self, Enlarge/Reduce, Summon Monstrosity. Level 9: Haste. Level 13: Freedom of Movement, Stoneskin. Level 17: Modify Memory, Reincarnate.",
  "Monstrous Eidolon": "You shape your Eidolon into a unique creature with Transmutation magic. **Changes.** Its type is Monstrosity. When you gain this feature, assign 13 (+1), 14 (+2), and 16 (+3) among its Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution. It gains two skill proficiencies of your choice, and you can swap one whenever you gain a level in this class. **Evolutions.** It has 2 more Evolutions, and gains another at levels 10 and 14. You can also pick from an expanded pool called Monstrous Evolutions, listed at the end of this subclass in the book.",
  "Transmutation Expert": "Conjuration Expert also covers Transmutation spells. Wizard Transmutation spells are added to your Summoner spell list.",
  "Reshape": "**Swap Evolution.** After a Long Rest you can swap one of your Eidolon's Evolutions for another it qualifies for. **Altered Self.** You do not need to concentrate on Alter Self.",
  "Monstrous Focus": "While you concentrate on a Conjuration or Transmutation spell and fail a save to keep Concentration, you can use your Reaction to reroll the save and must use the new roll.",
  "Master Reshaper": "After a Long Rest you can swap any number of your Eidolon's Evolutions. As a Magic action you can also trade one Evolution for another. You can do this a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum 1) and a Long Rest restores all uses."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Master Reshaper", "lvl": 14, "max": "mod:CHA", "reset": "long", "tag": "Magic action"}],
 "acts": {"Master Reshaper": "action", "Monstrous Focus": "reaction"}},

"Bond of the Shambling Plant": {"spab": "CHA",
 "f": {
  "Plant Spells": "At the Summoner levels in the table you always have these spells prepared. Level 3: Entangle, Goodberry. Level 5: Barkskin, Spike Growth, Summon Plant. Level 9: Plant Growth. Level 13: Conjure Woodland Beings, Grasping Vine. Level 17: Awaken, Tree Stride.",
  "Plant Eidolon": "Your Eidolon is a living plant of a kind you choose, able to move and talk. **Changes.** Its type is Plant. Strength 14 (+2), Dexterity 13 (+1), Constitution 16 (+3). It is proficient in Nature and Survival. **Sturdy.** It cannot be forcibly moved or knocked Prone against its will. **Ingrain (Bonus Action, cost 1 AP).** Its Speed becomes 0 and the ground in a 10-foot Emanation around it becomes Difficult Terrain for everyone except you and your allies. Using it again while Ingrained ends the effect. It also ends if the Eidolon leaves its space for any reason.",
  "Natural Spellcasting": "You can use a Druidic Focus for your Summoner spells. Pick one Druid cantrip and one level 1 Druid spell. You learn the cantrip without it counting against your cantrips known, and you always have the level 1 spell prepared. When you gain a level in this class, you can replace the cantrip with another Druid cantrip, and the spell with another Druid spell of any level you can prepare as a Summoner.",
  "Absorb Nutrients": "Your Eidolon gains the action Absorb Nutrients (cost 1 AP). One creature in the Difficult Terrain from Ingrain makes a Constitution save against your spell save DC. On a failure it takes 2d8 Necrotic damage, half on a success. Either way you regain Hit Points equal to the Necrotic damage dealt. The damage becomes 3d8 at level 10 and 4d8 at level 14. The Eidolon can also use this when not Ingrained, if it stands on rich soil. Then it deals no damage and you regain the maximum possible Hit Points. Uses equal your Charisma modifier (minimum 1). A Long Rest restores all.",
  "Reaching Roots": "**Increased Area.** The Ingrain Emanation becomes 20 feet. **Increased Reach.** While Ingrained, the Eidolon's Conjured Strike has 20 feet of reach. **Grasping Strike.** If the Eidolon damages a creature standing in the Difficult Terrain with Conjured Strike or Absorb Nutrients, that creature cannot leave the Difficult Terrain by moving until the end of its next turn.",
  "Root Network": "You always have Transport via Plants prepared, and your Eidolon counts as a valid plant to travel through. As a Magic action you can strengthen the link between you and your Eidolon for 1 hour. Your allies of your size or smaller can spend 5 feet of movement to teleport from a space within 5 feet of you or the Eidolon to an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the other, if you are no more than 60 feet apart, or 120 feet if the Eidolon is Ingrained. An ally cannot do this again until the start of its next turn. After you use the action you cannot use it again until a Short or Long Rest, unless you expend a level 4+ spell slot."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Absorb Nutrients", "lvl": 6, "max": "mod:CHA", "reset": "long", "tag": "1 AP"},
        {"feature": "Root Network", "lvl": 14, "max": 1, "reset": "short", "tag": "1 hour"}],
 "acts": {"Root Network": "action"}},

"Bond of the Spirit Animal": {"spab": "CHA",
 "f": {
  "Spirit Animal Spells": "At the Summoner levels in the table you always have these spells prepared. Level 3: Protection from Evil and Good, Shield, Summon Beast. Level 5: Pass without Trace. Level 9: Conjure Animals, Dispel Magic. Level 13: Conjure Woodland Beings, Polymorph. Level 17: Antilife Shell, Greater Restoration.",
  "Spirit Animal Eidolon": "Your Eidolon is a spectral animal of your choice, plainly supernatural. **Changes.** Its type is Beast. **Spirit Animal Kind.** Pick one when you gain this subclass. It sets the Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution scores and skill proficiencies. Cunning: 13 (+1), 16 (+3), 14 (+2), Sleight of Hand and Stealth. Grace: 14 (+2), 13 (+1), 16 (+3), Insight and Persuasion. Power: 16 (+3), 13 (+1), 14 (+2), Acrobatics and Athletics. Wisdom: 13 (+1), 16 (+3), 14 (+2), Insight and Perception. **Protective Field (cost 2 AP).** A 10-foot Emanation centered on the Eidolon lasts 1 minute or until it is Incapacitated. The first time a hostile creature tries to enter it on a turn, it makes a Charisma save against your spell save DC or is magically barred from entering until the start of its next turn. Uses equal your Charisma modifier (minimum 1). A Short Rest restores one use and a Long Rest restores all. **Changing kind.** The kind reflects your values and normally cannot change. After a profound change in your identity, your DM may allow it.",
  "Abjuration Expert": "Conjuration Expert also covers Abjuration spells. Wizard Abjuration spells are added to your Summoner spell list.",
  "Guardian's Fortitude": "Protective Field improves by Kind for friendly creatures in the Emanation. Cunning: Advantage on Dexterity and Intelligence saves. Grace: they have Cover. Power: Advantage on Strength and Constitution saves. Wisdom: Advantage on Wisdom and Charisma saves.",
  "Totemic Protection": "When you cast one of your Spirit Animal spells or a level 1+ Abjuration spell, spiritual energy wraps your body. Until the start of your next turn, the Protective Field also appears as a 5-foot Emanation centered on you.",
  "Guardian's Sanctuary": "Protective Field grows to a 20-foot Emanation, and Guardian's Fortitude improves by Kind. Cunning or Power: a friendly creature in the Emanation that succeeds on a save made with Advantage from Guardian's Fortitude takes no damage from the effect. Grace: when a friendly creature in the Emanation takes damage, reduce it by your Charisma modifier (minimum 1). Wisdom: friendly creatures in the Emanation have Resistance to Psychic damage and Immunity to the Charmed and Frightened conditions."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Spirit Animal Eidolon", "n": "Protective Field", "lvl": 3, "max": "mod:CHA", "reset": "long", "tag": "2 AP, Short Rest restores 1"}],
 "acts": {}},

"Bond of the Wrathful Giant": {"spab": "CHA",
 "f": {
  "Giant Spells": "At the Summoner levels in the table you always have these spells prepared. Level 3: Jump, Longstrider. Level 5: Enhance Ability, Enlarge/Reduce. Level 9: Conjure Barrage, Glyph of Warding. Level 11: Summon Giant. Level 13: Death Ward, Freedom of Movement. Level 17: Bigby's Hand.",
  "Giant Eidolon": "Your Eidolon is a Large humanoid giant, 10 to 13 feet tall, with exaggerated features you describe. **Changes.** Its type is Giant and its size is Large. Strength 17 (+3), Constitution 14 (+2). Its base Speed is 40 feet. It is proficient in Athletics. **Tough.** When you manifest it, add your Charisma modifier (minimum +1) to its starting Temporary Hit Points. **Powerful Strikes.** The d6s of its Conjured Strike become d8s, and the d4s of Ranged Attacker become d6s. At level 10 the d8s become d10s and the Ranged Attacker dice become d8s.",
  "Attuned Toughness": "You know Giant. Whenever you manifest your Eidolon, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to half your Summoner level (round up).",
  "Physical Empowerment": "When you sacrifice your action to give your Eidolon AP, you can also give it Advantage on D20 Tests with Strength and on its Conjured Strike attacks until the start of your next turn. Uses equal your Charisma modifier (minimum 1). A Long Rest restores all.",
  "Titanic Body": "**Titanic Size.** If you cast Enlarge/Reduce on only your Eidolon, you do not need Concentration. **Uncanny Constitution.** When an effect lets it make a Constitution save for half damage, it takes no damage on a success and half on a failure.",
  "Ultimate Empowerment": "**Quick Empowerment.** You can use Physical Empowerment when you sacrifice your Bonus Action to give your Eidolon AP. **Endless Empowerment.** If you sacrifice both your action and Bonus Action in one turn, you can use Physical Empowerment without spending a use."},
 "lu": [{"feature": "Physical Empowerment", "lvl": 6, "max": "mod:CHA", "reset": "long", "tag": "Advantage"}],
 "acts": {},
 "fx": [[3, "Attuned Toughness", {"langs": ["Giant"]}]]},
}
